        "original_id": "8383d1fb-bb85-5ce1-bfe3-974d878b2e10",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: R-26 salon\n- People: Josephine Baker, Le Corbusier, Django Reinhardt, Marie-Jacques Perrier, Robert Perrier\n- Roles: singer, architect, musician, composer, haute couture textile supplier\n- Concepts: Jazz Age, 1920s, artistic salon\n\nFacts:\n- On 1 January 1930, the R-26 salon was first convened.\n- Over the next eighty years, the R-26 salon became a meeting ground for creative luminaries including singer Josephine Baker, architect Le Corbusier, and musician Django Reinhardt.\n- Josephine Baker’s costume consisting only of a girdle of bananas became her most iconic image and a symbol of the Jazz Age and the 1920s.\n- Robert Perrier was a musical composer and a haute couture textile supplier.\n- Marie-Jacques Perrier was the daughter of Robert Perrier.\n- Marie-Jacques Perrier inherited direction of the R-26 artistic salon from Robert Perrier.",
